# ADR: Canonical cast with derived media and a Pages player

## Status
Accepted

## Context
Plan 8 needs a real model-backed demo that works in script-hostile README rendering, remains interactive elsewhere, leaks no recorder-machine context, and can be rebuilt without spending API tokens.

## Decision
Commit a privacy-scanned asciicast v2 file as the canonical source. Derive a script-free animated SVG and GIF with pinned renderers, enforce byte stability in CI, and host the official pinned player from the main-branch docs directory. The hero, piped ask, and explain use real Responses API calls; exact-intent aliases make dry-run bytes and cancellation deterministic. Recorder-added command and timestamp fields are removed before privacy scanning.

The model prompt now distinguishes ordinary pipelines from process control and routes undeclared directory traversal to shell tools, fixing issues discovered in the first live take.

## Alternatives Considered
- Anonymous asciinema.org upload: rejected as the canonical link because unclaimed uploads expire after seven days.
- Script inside the README SVG: rejected because GitHub sanitizes script content.
- Mocked model output: rejected because it would not demonstrate the product contract.

## Consequences
The README animation works without JavaScript, the Pages view is pausable and copyable, and CI can verify media with no API key. Re-recording still requires a key and human review; the Pages wrapper depends on pinned jsDelivr-hosted player assets.
